OL,3,GNEWSAPotential for pine martens'
OL,4,Areturn, findings show
OL,5,
OL,6,FThere is potential for pine martens to
OL,7,Freturn to their former habitats in
OL,8,Fsouth-east England, new research has
OL,9,Fshown.
OL,11,FThe pine marten, a cat-sized animal
OL,12,Ffrom the weasel family, became extinct
OL,13,Fin most of England and Wales in the
OL,14,Fearly 20th Century, according to Kent
OL,15,FWildlife Trust.
OL,17,FHowever, a study as part of the South
OL,18,FEast Pine Marten Restoration Project
OL,19,Fshows that the animal is most likely to
OL,20,Fthrive in areas with extensive woodland
OL,21,Fcover, with suitable habitats
OL,22,Fidentified in the region.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,323,320,200,140,0,100
